const decisions={
 'AI':['Recognize computer-performed tasks associated with human intelligence, including pattern recognition.','Qualified as introductory AI vocabulary, not proof of intelligence, accuracy or security.','No AI/ML identity union, universal reasoning, harmless output, autonomous suitability or tested model capability.'],
 'API':['Recognize an interface contract for application communication.','Qualified as interface vocabulary, without requiring remote network communication.','No automatic authentication, authorization, encryption, reliable data or secure implementation; APIs may be local or remote.'],
 'BIOS':['Recognize legacy boot firmware initializing hardware before operating-system loading.','Qualified as BIOS vocabulary, distinct from modern UEFI and the operating system.','Not every current device uses legacy BIOS; no firmware integrity, Secure Boot, measured boot or boot-chain validation is proved.'],
 'BYOD / COPE / CYOD':['Recognize the three expansions but hold the complete combined ownership-model card.','HOLD: the meaning only announces different security/privacy tradeoffs; it does not distinguish personally owned work devices, corporate-owned personally enabled devices, or selection from an approved device catalogue.','CYOD choice does not by itself establish ownership; organizational policy governs management/visibility/wipe authority and personal-data protections. Expansions alone do not teach these distinctions.'],
 'CASB':['Recognize a cloud-access policy-enforcement broker between users and cloud services.','Qualified as a logical policy-broker role, not necessarily an inline proxy for every request.','CASBs may use API/log/proxy integrations; they do not replace provider duties, IAM or protect every unmanaged/encrypted path automatically. No cloud provider/CASB identity merge.'],
 'DEP':['Recognize non-executable memory-page enforcement that makes injected-code exploitation harder.','Qualified with the source’s helps boundary, not prevention of every exploit.','DEP does not prevent every overwrite, code-reuse attack or executable-page abuse; platform/process policy and permitted executable regions matter. No memory or exploit execution.'],
 'DLL':['Recognize a reusable dynamically linked Windows module with code/functions and potentially data.','Qualified as shared-library vocabulary, not a claim every DLL is used by multiple programs concurrently.','No automatic trust, safe search/loading, dependency integrity or cross-platform equivalence; no library execution or hijacking test.'],
 'EDR':['Recognize endpoint monitoring with investigation and containment/response support.','Qualified as detection plus response support, not monitoring alone or guaranteed automatic containment.','Telemetry, configuration, operating system, access and service capabilities govern coverage and response; no detection rate or endpoint health is proved.'],
 'EFS / FDE':['Recognize the ordered contrast: EFS protects files; FDE protects disk/volume data at rest.','Qualified as file-versus-volume encryption vocabulary, not identical scopes or protection of every physical sector.','Windows EFS protects selected NTFS files; disk encryption targets supported volumes and can leave boot partitions unencrypted. Authorized/unlocked reads expose plaintext; neither replaces access policy or protects an already compromised running host.'],
 'GPU':['Recognize a graphics processor also used for parallel compute such as ML and some password guessing.','Qualified as a processor/workload example, not a universal cracking capability.','Performance depends on workload/algorithm/memory/hardware; GPUs do not automatically recover passwords, break encryption or establish AI accuracy.'],
 'HDD / SSD':['Recognize spinning/mechanical storage versus common flash-based solid-state storage.','Qualified as common device-type vocabulary, without universal speed, durability or sanitization claims.','Flash SSD is the common implementation; the SSD category is not a universal memory-technology guarantee. Wear leveling, controller behavior and media limits matter for disposal; no sanitization or drive test.'],
 'HIDS / NIDS':['Recognize host-based versus network-based suspicious-activity detection in the ordered compound face.','Qualified as detection-location vocabulary; the shared IDS suffix applies to both named components.','Visibility, telemetry, encrypted traffic and false positives limit detection. Neither automatically blocks all attacks or supplies a complete response; no detection benchmark.'],
 'HIPS / NIPS':['Recognize host-based versus network-based prevention mechanisms that can block suspicious activity.','Qualified with can-block wording; the shared IPS suffix applies to both components.','Blocking is policy/deployment dependent and can cause false positives or availability costs; no complete prevention guarantee, IDS/IPS identity union or network execution.'],
 'IaaS / PaaS / SaaS':['Recognize expansions but hold the complete combined cloud-service-model card.','HOLD: different responsibility split supplies no individual service capability or customer/provider control boundary for IaaS, PaaS and SaaS.','IaaS offers fundamental compute with customer OS/apps; PaaS hosts customer apps on provider platforms; SaaS offers provider apps with limited configuration. Those omitted distinctions cannot be transferred from the separately reviewed shared-responsibility card.'],
 'IaC':['Recognize infrastructure configuration expressed in code/files rather than manual configuration.','Qualified as an infrastructure-management mechanism, not a security assurance or mandatory reviewed-file claim.','Automation can propagate insecure changes; review, policy, access/secrets handling, testing and drift controls remain separate. The earlier IaC guide-entry hold stays unresolved.'],
 'IoT':['Recognize network-connected physical devices such as sensors and cameras.','Qualified as introductory connected-device vocabulary with examples, not a claim every host is IoT or must directly use the public internet.','Definitions vary by publication; sensing/actuation and network/data context matter. No IoT/OT/ICS identity union, default security, lifecycle support or device configuration assessment.']
};
